  "body": "## Summary\n\nOffer three existing tools in the local chat core set:\n- `rename_operation`\n- `edit_tool`\n- `set_work_material`\n\nKeep the existing 25 tools. The provider still reads each schema from the live MCP registry. Tool behavior, validation, confirmation gates and undo commands do not change.\n\n## Reproduction before the fix\n\nBaseline: `9b141e1122fad4aca12e6502dd5f4963209b4e68` on upstream `main`.\n\nThe regression tests ran before the core list changed:\n- `every_live_tool_maps_without_schema_loss` failed: `Core lacks rename_operation`.\n- The local panel exposure test failed: `local payload lacks rename_operation`.\n- The native rename test failed: `rename must be offered`.\n\n## Tests\n\nLinux, Rust, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3`, existing development toolchain. No network inference.\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_provider --test mcp_compact`: 16 tests passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib egui_app::tests::ai_chat:: -- --test-threads=3`: 66 tests passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: all 15 steps passed, including the full app and UI lib suites.\n- All 11 light twins passed. Ran the five test steps with `cargo xtask gate light --base origin/main --only 'motion light' --only 'app light'`. Omitted only the broad release prebuild. The final app step exceeded a tool timeout; `--only 'app light'` then passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 3 -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo clippy -j 3 -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nThe provider test checks Full and Core schemas in Anthropic, OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses and Gemini formats. The panel test lists all three tools in local Native and Prompt-JSON requests.\n\nThe new native panel test runs `rename_operation` through the real worker and live MCP inbox. It checks `Face1` becomes `Roughing`, retains its stable key, returns the tool result and adds one history entry. Undo Turn restores `Face1` and the original history depth. The existing core schema budget still passes: less than one third of the full table.\n\n## Limits and decisions\n\nThis deterministic test shows that the benchmark rename task can execute. It does not claim a rerun of the 12 real models. No live model setup, machining algorithms, parameter semantics, G-code, collision checks or visible UI layout changed. No screenshot or example-catalog run applies to this tool-table change. Full heavy lanes and release packaging were not run. The graphify executable is not installed.\n\nNo scout was commissioned. Bounded direct reads located the core list, provider schemas, registry entries, panel budget test and undo helpers. Open PR file lists showed no overlap in the changed paths. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3546-chat-core-tools.md`.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3546#issuecomment-7209713622\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: Local AI chat offers the existing operation rename, tool edit and work material tools.\n\nFixes #3546\n",
